Package: hyperflux-next-v2-linux
Architecture: amd64
Depends: systemd,
         udev,
         ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends}
Provides: hyperflux-next-dkms (= ${binary:Version}),
          hyperflux-next-linux (= ${binary:Version})
Conflicts: hyperflux-next-dkms, hyperflux-next-linux, hyperflux-v2-linux-dkms
Replaces: hyperflux-next-dkms, hyperflux-next-linux, hyperflux-v2-linux-dkms
Description: HyperFlux Next V2 bridge, CLI and base services
 The HyperFlux Next V2 bridge and device keeper services, the hyperfluxctl
 command, and the system users, sockets and udev rules they need. The
 bridge reaches the Razer HyperFlux V2 receiver (USB 1532:00cf) through
 hidraw, and the batteries of the devices paired to it show up in the
 desktop's battery widget. It takes over from the hyperflux-next-linux
 package and the receiver kernel modules of earlier releases.
 .
 This is the Core edition. Install hyperflux-next-v2-full to use the
 devices in OpenRazer apps, and hyperflux-next-v2-openrgb-plugin for
 OpenRGB.

Package: hyperflux-next-v2-openrazer-driver-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends: dkms,
         systemd,
         udev,
         ${misc:Depends}
Provides: hyperflux-next-openrazer-driver-dkms (= ${binary:Version}),
          hyperflux-openrazer-driver-abi (= 3.12.4),
          openrazer-driver-dkms (= 3.12.4+dfsg-1),
          openrazer-kernel-modules-dkms
Conflicts: hyperflux-next-openrazer-driver-dkms, openrazer-driver-dkms, openrazer-kernel-modules-dkms
Replaces: hyperflux-next-openrazer-driver-dkms, openrazer-driver-dkms, openrazer-kernel-modules-dkms
Description: OpenRazer driver sources with the HyperFlux Next V2 transport, for DKMS
 OpenRazer 3.12.4's kernel drivers with the patches that let them drive
 the devices HyperFlux Next V2 offers. It takes the place of the
 distribution's openrazer-driver-dkms, so the stock openrazer-daemon
 installs on top of it.

Package: hyperflux-next-v2-full
Architecture: all
Depends: hyperflux-next-v2-linux (= ${source:Version}),
         hyperflux-next-v2-openrazer-driver-dkms (= ${source:Version}),
         ${hfx:Full-Depends},
         ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: ${hfx:Full-Recommends}
Provides: hyperflux-next-full (= ${binary:Version})
Conflicts: hyperflux-next-full
Replaces: hyperflux-next-full
Suggests: openrazer-daemon, python3-openrazer
Description: HyperFlux Next V2 Core plus OpenRazer support for the paired devices
 The udev rules and module list that let the HyperFlux Next V2 bridge offer
 the paired devices to OpenRazer apps such as Polychromatic. On Debian it
 also brings the OpenRGB plugin, which Debian's own OpenRGB loads.

Package: hyperflux-next-v2-openrgb-plugin
Architecture: amd64
Depends: hyperflux-next-v2-linux (= ${binary:Version}),
         ${hfx:OpenRGB},
         ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends}
Enhances: openrgb
# The old hyperflux-next-full carried a plugin. This lets apt unpack the
# new one before it has removed the old package.
Replaces: hyperflux-next-full (<< 1:1.0.1~)
Description: HyperFlux Next V2 plugin for OpenRGB
 Shows the Razer devices paired with a HyperFlux V2 receiver in OpenRGB,
 and adds a page with their batteries to OpenRGB's Information tab.
 .
 The Debian package is built for Debian's own OpenRGB 1.0. The Ubuntu
 package is built for OpenRGB 1.1 from openrgb.org and depends on it,
 because Ubuntu's own OpenRGB is too old to load the plugin.
